                        ],
                        "form": "кро́ве"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "bf0c36a3-d651-4575-bdea-6eca21b5cc6b",
                        "entry_id": "28326b5e-08fa-387d-9e1a-4f1712780104",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "prepositional"
                        ],
                        "form": "кро́вах"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ef8606a8-44e7-3bdb-aeb7-b9d1d87d77d6",
                        "entry_id": "28326b5e-08fa-387d-9e1a-4f1712780104",
                        "glosses": [
                            "устар. крыша, укрытие, навес"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d8b59ad5-4936-4708-9653-490089c302be",
                                "sense_id": "ef8606a8-44e7-3bdb-aeb7-b9d1d87d77d6",
                                "text": "Я вступил в тёмную аллею, под кров шумящих дубов и с некоторым благоговением углублялся во мрак её."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "75f730e0-35a3-4a53-a403-5e05c61a0390",
                                "sense_id": "ef8606a8-44e7-3bdb-aeb7-b9d1d87d77d6",
                                "text": "У нас не найдёшь, мой друг, // Ни злата, ни мраморов // Под кровом соломенным;"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "850ba1f9-7067-37a7-9672-98a1f19bf609",
                        "entry_id": "28326b5e-08fa-387d-9e1a-4f1712780104",
                        "glosses": [
                            "перен. защита"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "02496d74-4f49-40cd-aa2b-db215806d993",
                                "sense_id": "850ba1f9-7067-37a7-9672-98a1f19bf609",
                                "text": "― Так исполни последнюю просьбу мою, последнее мое приказание: оставь нас под кровом божиим и возьми с собою благословение матери."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "bec167eb-5581-3bbe-b22d-807c30cd56ec",
                        "entry_id": "28326b5e-08fa-387d-9e1a-4f1712780104",
                        "glosses": [
                            "книжн. дом, жилище, приют"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e06229cc-8562-49e2-a9b0-3d1da1d11a2e",
                                "sense_id": "bec167eb-5581-3bbe-b22d-807c30cd56ec",
                                "text": "Теплый и уютный кров, мягкая постель, превосходный стол, просторные комнаты с мебелью, самая необходимая одежда, ванна, книги, фортепьяно, бумага и чернила заключали в себе все земные блага, и, наверное, я более других способна была оценить оные."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2d2a4588-2a6c-4a7f-a706-4af94badd800",
                                "sense_id": "bec167eb-5581-3bbe-b22d-807c30cd56ec",
                                "text": "Нет, Маша, я не могу позволить тебе уйти отсюда… Здесь твоё гнездо, твой кров; здесь всё твое и всё для тебя — я не могу с тобой расстаться…"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "1b4415d5-57bc-4e2c-81b2-c26e0f82db31",
                        "source_entry_id": "28326b5e-08fa-387d-9e1a-4f1712780104",
                        "source_sense_description": "крыша, навес",
                        "target_lang_word": "roof",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "roof",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3977c5a0-404c-330b-9b7c-ae48a9a4f367",
                                        "entry_id": "e4c2bf1d-1490-3896-b299-4cd8180eaf71",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The external covering at the top of a building."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "985d8299-0dda-409d-9cc2-4d1d338767d8",
                                                "sense_id": "3977c5a0-404c-330b-9b7c-ae48a9a4f367",
                                                "text": "The roof was blown off by the tornado."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dd5b2b9c-8382-4483-a377-3c52b1406b7a",
                                                "sense_id": "3977c5a0-404c-330b-9b7c-ae48a9a4f367",
                                                "text": "'Twas the house I'd seen the roof of from the beach."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ea695c1a-f82b-4f32-8f9c-c86c1bf776fb",
                                                "sense_id": "3977c5a0-404c-330b-9b7c-ae48a9a4f367",
                                                "text": "The very first sound that you’ll hear on the roof\n(Provided there’s fog) will be Rudolph’s small hoof."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7f4dc374-9cbe-4813-9ea3-6dcd92c72411",
                                                "sense_id": "3977c5a0-404c-330b-9b7c-ae48a9a4f367",
                                                "text": "The roof, the roof, the roof is on fire!\nWe don't need no water: Let the motherfucker burn!\nBurn, motherfucker, burn!"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d4be1d47-6504-371c-883a-008d540a20eb",
                                        "entry_id": "e4c2bf1d-1490-3896-b299-4cd8180eaf71",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The top external level of a building."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "53a74575-0bd8-4d56-ac6c-73300cb0ee9a",
                                                "sense_id": "d4be1d47-6504-371c-883a-008d540a20eb",
                                                "text": "Let's go up to the roof."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f714ac2e-16e5-4a34-878c-8297086042d1",
                                                "sense_id": "d4be1d47-6504-371c-883a-008d540a20eb",
                                                "text": "When this old world starts getting me down\nAnd people are just too much for me to face,\nI climb way up to the top of the stairs\nAnd all my cares just drift right into space\nOn the roof, it's peaceful as can be\nAnd there, the world below can't bother me..."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cb1f8d18-e06d-370c-bd18-2c8adf15987f",
                                        "entry_id": "e4c2bf1d-1490-3896-b299-4cd8180eaf71",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The upper part of a cavity."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "075f75f1-d949-43e6-8a44-c87ad5af6f73",
                                                "sense_id": "cb1f8d18-e06d-370c-bd18-2c8adf15987f",
                                                "text": "The palate is the roof of the mouth."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "79cda346-3a24-48f8-8055-7a099d82e37d",
                                                "sense_id": "cb1f8d18-e06d-370c-bd18-2c8adf15987f",
                                                "text": "As Bent pulled away to the far post, Agbonlahor opted to go it alone, motoring past Gary Caldwell before unleashing a shot into the roof of the net."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a243d75a-aab4-31a8-922f-29baa954d2be",
                                        "entry_id": "e4c2bf1d-1490-3896-b299-4cd8180eaf71",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The surface or bed of rock immediately overlying a bed of coal or a flat vein."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b579aaad-9bf5-38cf-b9c5-997c965ca8af",
                                        "entry_id": "e4c2bf1d-1490-3896-b299-4cd8180eaf71",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An overhanging rock wall."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "418437aa-55a3-30ed-a7aa-98e316f9d332",
                                        "entry_id": "e4c2bf1d-1490-3896-b299-4cd8180eaf71",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A hat."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic",
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1d62dc14-9e04-434d-a26b-4ff6719654f7",
                                                "sense_id": "418437aa-55a3-30ed-a7aa-98e316f9d332",
                                                "text": "Tom thought his cap a very knowing affair, but confessed that he had a hat in his hat-box; which was accordingly at once extracted from the hind-boot, and Tom equipped in his go-to-meeting roof, as his new friend called it."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "roof",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fd2091be-f73d-3c12-94ab-241b73604fac",
                                        "entry_id": "9f090326-10b5-33d7-aa65-569fee8727fd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To cover or furnish with a roof."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "edacde8f-c3e8-48e7-b577-3bedf4719c85",
                                                "sense_id": "fd2091be-f73d-3c12-94ab-241b73604fac",
                                                "text": "A trench about ten feet deep was dug in the ground and roofed over with sticks and earth so as to form a dark tunnel."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "dd6076b7-b187-3ecd-8225-7dd2d837720a",
                                        "entry_id": "9f090326-10b5-33d7-aa65-569fee8727fd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To traverse buildings by walking or climbing across their roofs."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f8d2b3b7-e120-3f67-8ddf-fd7da63cfbcf",
                                        "entry_id": "9f090326-10b5-33d7-aa65-569fee8727fd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To put into prison, to bird."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "slang",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8bbbe12b-1ee4-4cb5-b29c-47bab2612bca",
                                                "sense_id": "f8d2b3b7-e120-3f67-8ddf-fd7da63cfbcf",
                                                "text": "Did you see them, David? I mean, did you see them looking at me? I-I'm walking out of the court, and everybody was practically – yeah, they were gawking. […] I mean, Noah roofed me, I proved it, end of story."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2398106b-1ad7-46ae-a4a8-aa8309bab03f",
                                                "sense_id": "f8d2b3b7-e120-3f67-8ddf-fd7da63cfbcf",
                                                "text": "I’m open, hype off the chronic I was smoking, feeling zooted\nThat Brooklyn shit got me stupid\nI’m loose, kid – that’s what the overproof did\nWhat the ruck you looking at, son? You’ll get roofed, kid!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "20f6933d-a2d5-4074-93b7-73d7f5a1eb00",
                                                "sense_id": "f8d2b3b7-e120-3f67-8ddf-fd7da63cfbcf",
                                                "text": "Inhale the mystical, the blue shit\nSee me on the stoop shit, act stupid at the park, the ball, get roofed\nBaby see the cops, the drugs, she boofed it\nFoie gras at every meal, that means I triple-goosed it"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "86e3a464-e856-4eea-9b0f-2652f13320c2",
                                                "sense_id": "f8d2b3b7-e120-3f67-8ddf-fd7da63cfbcf",
                                                "text": "You don’t want war, you’re shook of it\nHella man dash when their friend got roofed"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "513d5e50-5ed5-36e5-9dcd-7c8a0356d7a9",
                                        "entry_id": "9f090326-10b5-33d7-aa65-569fee8727fd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To shelter as if under a roof."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3260c805-9116-40e0-832d-5c2825fbd5ff",
                                                "sense_id": "513d5e50-5ed5-36e5-9dcd-7c8a0356d7a9",
                                                "text": "They reached him: the pieces of rock had roofed him over—he was without injury or scratch."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "33279a2e-dec8-425c-80dc-c0b19fe8fe7d",
                                                "sense_id": "513d5e50-5ed5-36e5-9dcd-7c8a0356d7a9",
